{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `log_radon`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual likelihood accumulation inside the loop, `target += normal_lpdf(log_radon[n] | mu[n], sigma_y)`, with a single built-in vectorized sampling statement, `log_radon ~ normal(mu, sigma_y)`. The linear predictor `mu` is still computed deterministically from parameters and context data before the observation statement. This preserves the same normal likelihood while satisfying SafeStan's requirement that protected data be observed exactly once with a plain top-level sampling statement. No data fields were added or changed.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0> J;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county_idx;
  vector[N] floor_measure;
  vector[N] log_radon;
}
parameters {
  vector[J] alpha;
  real beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
}
model {
  vector[N] mu;
  // Prior
  sigma_y ~ normal(0, 1);
  alpha ~ normal(0, 10);
  beta ~ normal(0, 10);

  // Likelihood
  for (n in 1 : N) {
    mu[n] = alpha[county_idx[n]] + beta * floor_measure[n];
  }
  log_radon ~ normal(mu, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":1,"N":3,"county_idx":[1,1,1],"floor_measure":[6.424545828586487,2.7455458090030556,4.96770362271589],"log_radon":[6.521361489321556,5.141051227383004,5.644358432913151]}","protected_variables":["log_radon"]}
